* Program-select bench: one cell, nfet_06v0 select in series with the fuse.
* Circuit body for `klt sim` (no .control/.end). run.sh substitutes @DESIGN@,
* @RROUTE@ and @FUSE@ and writes the result into the record directory.
.include @DESIGN@
* The PDK efuse subcircuit (pblow=0 -> 200 ohm) comes from the `efuse` section
* of the model library, added to every corner as a second section by the
* request (not through a res_* process block, so it does not depend on the
* process corner name).

* ASSUMPTION (no documented source): routing resistance, one lumped value in
* series with the fuse. Single parameter, set only in run.sh.
.param rroute=@RROUTE@
* Select width; run.sh writes one deck per width.
.param wsel=@WSEL@
* Plain-resistor fuse variants (140 / 260) are written with the value inline.
* Program supply; klt sim alters source Vdd per corner (4.5 / 5.0 / 5.5 V).
.param vdd=5.0

Vdd vdd 0 DC {vdd}
* ASSUMPTION (ideal level-shifter output): gate = program supply at that
* corner, so Vgs tracks the supply. Ideal VCVS, no output resistance.
Eg g 0 vdd 0 1
* Zero-volt ammeter in the supply leg: fuse current = i(Vi) (run.sh measures it as the Rr drop / rroute).
Vi vdd na DC 0
@FUSE@
Rr nb d {rroute}
Xsel d g 0 0 nfet_06v0 w={wsel} l=0.7u
* Unused two-point sweep axis: plain .meas cards need a dc sweep, and the
* fuse current is read at its first point (every point is the same bias).
Vdmy dmy 0 0
Rdmy dmy 0 1k
